 ],
 "notes": "PRIMARY SOURCE: official MENTOR US Product Catalog (Effective Jan 2019, PN 020827-181217) hosted on Mentor's own ordering portal mentordirect.com; identical 2020 edition is hosted on jnjmedtech.com. All source tables are published in CM (no mm conversion needed); diameter = base width for round implants. SURFACES DO NOT SHARE DIMENSIONS in the US line: SILTEX textured versions of the same profile/volume differ slightly from smooth (typically +0.1-0.2 cm diameter and +0.0-0.2 cm projection); both tables are provided per profile. Volume ranges: smooth Moderate Classic 130-800, Moderate Plus 100-800, High 125-800, Ultra High 135-800; SILTEX same except Ultra High 135-700 (matches FDA-approved size ranges in the MemoryGel labeling). FOOTNOTE printed on every table: 'Individual implant dimensions may vary slightly in products of this type. Not all units will conform exactly to the dimensions noted above.' (no numeric tolerance given). MemoryShape matrix is SILTEX microtextured only, Cohesive III gel; styles map to legacy CPG numbers: MM=321, MM+=322, MH=323, LM+=331, TM+=332, TH=333. Catalog also lists a Lower Pole Arc (A-B) dimension for shaped implants in some regional editions (not in the US catalog table); not included. OUT OF SCOPE but present in same catalog: MemoryGel Xtra (Moderate Plus Xtra, Moderate High Xtra, High Profile Xtra; smooth and SILTEX) and the new MemoryGel BOOST and MemoryGel Enhance (930-1445 cc, FDA-approved Dec 2024) lines - dimension tables for these were NOT extracted. GAPS: FDA P060028c product insert lists only Style MM ranges (original 2013 approval; other styles added via supplements, so no per-size FDA dimension table exists for MM+/MH/TM+/LM+/TH - catalog values cross-checked against regional Mentor catalogs instead). accessdata.fda.gov blocks direct download but the P060028c/P060028b PDFs were retrieved and read. No conflicts found between any sources; the only anomaly is the non-monotonic SILTEX Moderate Plus intermediate-size projections printed in the US catalog (transcribed verbatim)."
}